From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: avplumber patches <patches@local>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:21:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/hwupload_cuda: opt-in pinned staging and GPU v210
 unpack

Reuse the supplied CUDA context, stage software frames in pinned memory and copy on a private nonblocking stream. Preserve default transfers. GPU v210 unpack accepts gray-wrapped packed rows and requires a CUDA compiler; ordinary pinned upload does not. Synchronize before forwarding, and order pooled output reuse against the device stream.
---
 doc/filters.texi                |  22 +++
 libavfilter/Makefile            |   3 +
 libavfilter/vf_hwupload_cuda.c  | 233 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 libavfilter/vf_hwupload_cuda.cu |  83 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 336 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/vf_hwupload_cuda.cu

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 0167152..7f253e1 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -16164,6 +16164,28 @@ It accepts the following optional parameters:
 @table @option
 @item device
 The number of the CUDA device to use
+@item pinned
+Use reusable pinned host staging and a private nonblocking CUDA stream for
+software NV12/P010 uploads. Default is disabled. If a CUDA filter device is
+provided, reuse its context. Upload completion is synchronized before the
+output frame is forwarded; this option does not eliminate CPU waits.
+
+@item v210_width
+Treat gray input frames as packed v210 rows and unpack them on the GPU into
+linear frames of this picture width. The input width is the packed byte
+stride; it must be a multiple of 32 (v210 rows are padded to 128 bytes) and
+large enough for an even picture width. Zero disables unpacking (the default).
+This option implies pinned staging and requires a CUDA compiler at build time.
+It does not perform CPU v210 decoding. Set the source's color properties
+explicitly.
+
+@item v210_format
+The storage @option{v210_width} unpacks into, in the same pass: @code{p210le}
+(the default, every code as it is), @code{p010le} or @code{nv12}. The 8-bit
+samples of NV12 are rounded. A 4:2:0 chroma row is the rounded mean of its two
+picture rows, which in a frame flagged interlaced are the two nearest rows of
+the chroma row's own field.
+
 @end table
 
 @section hqx
